...in a locked shop??  That's going to be a long wait, especially as I
don't think the game will normally generate monsters in the same room
you're in.  And I believe without =oSD you'll get hungry again faster
than the prayer timout expires.

Of course, if you're lucky and wait long enough, some monster may open
the door for you... except I'm not sure if there are any monsters
generated at XL2/DL4 that can unlock or break doors.

My suggestion would be to try the potions.  You're in a shop, so you
can price-ID them first.  Cursed gain level could save you, and speed
might let you run away.  Or a smoky potion _might_ give a wish.  You
could even try alchemy to make more useful potions.

If that fails, try the poly wand.  Note that polying yourself into a
form with no hands is considered a major trouble, and can be cured by
praying.  If you do have hands, you can always toss objects upwards
until you run out of hit points and poly back -- or just wait it out.

If that doesn't work either, and you have no more un-ID'd objects to
test, just break the door and run for it.  What have you got to lose?

All that said, I wouldn't really give you very high odds of survival.
Just try to make the best of it, and if you do die anyway, just chalk
it up to bad luck and start again.

(Of course, having said that, someone else will now come up with an
obvious trick that will get you out safely and easily.)

